{
  "reason": "Commands whose replies hand out something with a remote lifetime: targets, contexts, sessions, worlds, scripts, remote objects and IO streams. A reply that arrives after its caller was interrupted, or timed out, is routed to an owner, which adopts or releases it (PROTOCOL.md, Protocol client). `release` names the commands that release it, from the CDP spec's own pairs: closeTarget, disposeBrowserContext, detachFromTarget, removeScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument, releaseObject and IO.close. An isolated world and a compiled script have no release command; they last as long as their document.",
